OL,3,GNEWSA'Different cultures look at autism
OL,4,Ain different ways'                     
OL,6,F"Chapatis are a no-go. While I was     
OL,7,Fgrowing up, my mum would say to me,    
OL,8,Fwhat are you going to do if your       
OL,9,Fhusband likes eating chapatis? I mean, 
OL,10,Fthat's our traditional food. I was     
OL,11,Flike, I don't know. He's going to have 
OL,12,Fto eat bread."                         
OL,14,FHina Shaikh, from Bradford, was        
OL,15,Fdiagnosed as autistic at the age of 42 
OL,16,Fafter years of struggling to understand
OL,17,Fwhy she felt different to everyone     
OL,18,Faround her.                            
